[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "_note": "Open. Default webcam view, one line of dialogue in the DEFAULT xp.css box — translucent beige, speaker name as a tab. `speech` is the rig's own chrome and the two \"default view\" scenes (this one and 12) are the only places the show uses it; the paper treatments are for the headers and the worn label. Scenes are SPARSE: omitting a field changes nothing, `null` removes, and saving through the panel will fatten them into fully-resolved absolute scenes.",
    "objects": {
      "cam": {
        "type": "webcam"
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "speech",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.8,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.92,
        "speaker": "shm",
        "text": "hi everyone. I'd like to read you a poem."
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 2,
    "_note": "THE POEM begins. `reset: true` clears the stage outright rather than nulling the webcam and the dialogue one at a time — the blackout IS the empty stage, because #stage is already black. Each of the next nine scenes adds exactly ONE line and restates nothing: a line inherited from the previous scene keeps its own DOM element and does not re-animate, while the line the scene ADDS is built fresh and its CSS fade fires once. There is no fade feature in the engine; that is the whole mechanism. Stanza 1 of 3.",
    "reset": true,
    "objects": {
      "poem1": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.13,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "i make myself a home in every seat i sit in three times,"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 3,
    "objects": {
      "poem2": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.205,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "every person i talk to twice,"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 4,
    "objects": {
      "poem3": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.28,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "every friend i cry with once."
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 5,
    "objects": {
      "poem4": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.355,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "i circle and settle in to rest."
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 6,
    "_note": "Stanza 2. The extra gap between y 0.355 and y 0.45 is the stanza break — spacing inside a stanza is 0.075, between stanzas it is wider.",
    "objects": {
      "poem5": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.45,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "i am surprised"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 7,
    "objects": {
      "poem6": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.525,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "every single time"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 8,
    "objects": {
      "poem7": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.6,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "to be jostled awake and told,"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 9,
    "objects": {
      "poem8": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.675,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "\"it's time to go\""
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 10,
    "objects": {
      "poem9": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.75,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "i wrest myself away in shock and horror…"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 11,
    "_note": "Stanza 3 — the last line, alone, after the widest gap in the poem.",
    "objects": {
      "poem10": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "poem",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.845,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.9,
        "instant": true,
        "text": "i will do it again."
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 12,
    "_note": "SUDDENLY — default view again, and the default xp.css box again. `reset: true` takes all ten lines and the blackout off in one stroke; ten separate nulls would do the same thing and read as a wall. The cut is meant to be abrupt, so nothing here fades.",
    "reset": true,
    "objects": {
      "cam": {
        "type": "webcam"
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "speech",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.8,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.92,
        "speaker": "shm",
        "text": "instead of speaking off a script for this one, I wanted to talk to everyone more directly, so instead, i've got a list of topics to address."
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 13,
    "_note": "THE TOPICS begin. `header` style: skinny centred cardstock at the TOP of the frame, Comic Sans, no speaker tab, `instant: true` so the typewriter never runs on it. Everything after this scene changes one field — `topic.text` — and nothing else, so the slip stays exactly put while the words change. Drop `y` to 0.8 if you would rather it sat at the bottom.",
    "objects": {
      "dialogue": null,
      "topic": {
        "type": "text",
        "style": "header",
        "x": 0.5,
        "y": 0.12,
        "z": 200,
        "width": 0.46,
        "instant": true,
        "tilt": 0,
        "text": "My Silly Puppet Stochastic Summer"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 14,
    "_note": "The sock puppet, lifted from CNMAT_openlab scene 14 — same assets, same numbers. A ventriloquy puppet is an ORDINARY image with two extra fields: `talkSrc` swaps the frame while you speak and `bounce` hops it, both driven by mic level. That is why it still takes `fasten` and can ride your hand. NEEDS THE MIC: config.json now sets micOnStart so \"it's showtime!\" asks for camera and mic together — without it the sock loads and simply never moves, which looks like a broken puppet rather than a missing permission. Assets 309/310 live in assets/CNMAT_openlab/, reached by number; copy them into assets/stochastic_final/ as 409/410 if you would rather this show owned them. CNMAT puts a second sock on the right hand (same object, `\"flipX\": true`) — one paste away if you want both.",
